      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can only hope that VRChat decides to move forward in that path, as multiple of my friends have been temp-banned for avatars that they've made being used in places they shouldn't.\n\n VRChat does not give them a chance to de-list the avatar or even explain themselves, they just go straight to measures like this, which only makes you fear the idea that it could happen to you too.\n\nI am not a big fan of giving websites my id and face-scans, however i've done it for VRChat, and i am age verified, which is good because now i can attend 18+ events, however it doesn't really change anything else!\n\nSo i genuinely pray for age restricted avatars, and worlds, just for the sake of losing that previously mentioned fear of a higher being striking you down, or striking down artist that genuinely spend days to work their craft.\n\nMost of the time, this isn't an act of moderation that protects people, like banning a malicious user, it's punishing people that attempt to work within your flawed system, people that try to find a home within a very complicated landscape on the internet and in real life. So please instead of banning users directly, fix your system, take the time to talk, and move forward in a way that is healthy for the adult community.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
