      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df1706d8e3ae44b28910e8|full_name}That's another bad vibe on top of everything, yeah. The \"how it is moderated.\" No warning, no force to private, just complete deletion and temp-ban. A friend even got unbanned again, as he poked the support. So it was not so bad to begin with? And support is a different section than mods, so they even don't really know?\n\nIf not already happening, mods should be forced to fill out a report why exactly a world needs to get taken down. We put weeks of work in it, I think they could do more than clicking a button, or using an AI that's not really differentiating or whatever. Give us reasons to learn and avoid in future at least and not \"cuz TOS.\" Wonderful. I'd love to get in court and instantly to jail, hearing \"cuz laws.\"\n\nTransparency would lower the current anger, that I see and read spreading everywhere these days...",
